# Laravel Naming

| Element | Convention | Good |
|---------|------------|------|
| Model | singular PascalCase | `BlogPost` |
| Controller | singular + `Controller` | `BlogPostController` |
| Route URL | plural | `/blog-posts` |
| Route name | snake_case + dots | `blog_posts.index` |
| Table | plural snake_case | `blog_posts` |
| Pivot | singular models, alpha | `article_user` |
| Column / FK | snake_case / `{model}_id` | `user_id` |
| Form Request | `{Action}{Model}Request` | `StoreBlogPostRequest` |
| Policy / Factory / Seeder | `{Model}{Suffix}` | `BlogPostPolicy` |
| Job | verb phrase | `SendWelcomeEmail` |
| Event | past tense | `OrderPlaced` |
| Service | `{Noun}Service` | `PaymentService` |
| Repo interface | `{Model}RepositoryInterface` | `BlogPostRepositoryInterface` |
| Repo impl | `Eloquent{Model}Repository` | `EloquentBlogPostRepository` |
| Action | verb phrase | `CreateBlogPost` |
| View | kebab-case | `show-filtered.blade.php` |
| Methods / vars | camelCase, descriptive | `$activeUsers` |

## Relationships

- `hasOne` / `belongsTo` → singular (`author`)
- `hasMany` / `belongsToMany` → plural (`comments`)

## Quality

- No `$data`, `$obj`, `$temp`; no type suffixes (`$userArray` → `$users`)
- Resource controllers use `index|store|show|update|destroy`
- Pest: `it('...')` / `test('...')` in plain English
